\v 10 Your¦85143 god¦85143 Yahweh¦85142 promised your¦85149 ancestors¦85149 Abraham¦85150,\x + \xo 6:10: \xt Gen 12:7.\x* Yitshak¦85151,\x + \xo 6:10: \xt Gen 26:3.\x* and¦85138 Yakov¦85152,\x + \xo 6:10: \xt Gen 28:13.\x* that he'd give¦85153 you large¦85156, \add ≈prosperous\add* cities¦85155 that you didn't¦85159 have to¦85149 build¦85161,
\v 11 houses¦85163 full¦85164 of¦85165 every¦85165 good¦85167 thing¦85167 that you didn't have to collect, wells¦85172 that you didn't have to dig, and vineyards¦85178 and olive¦85179 groves¦85179 that you didn't have to plant¦85183. You'll be able to eat¦85184 and be satisfied¦85185,
\v 12 \add but\add* be sure to¦85188 never forget¦85191 that¦85195 it was Yahweh¦85194 who¦85195 rescued you¦85196 from¦85197 slavery¦85200 in Egypt¦85198.
\v 13 You¦85206 must¦85206 honour your¦85205 god¦85205 Yahweh¦85204 and only serve¦85208 him¦85207 and only make promises using his¦85209 name¦85209.\x + \xo 6:13: \xt Mat 4:10; Luk 4:8.\x*
\v 14 Don't go \add ≈trying to follow\add* other¦85216 gods—the gods of¦85220 the surrounding countries—
\v 15 because¦85222 your¦85227 god Yahweh¦85225 who lives among you is¦85223 a jealous¦85224 god. You¦85233 wouldn't want \add *him\add* to get angry with¦85227 you and¦85236 \add ≈totally\add* destroy¦85236 you.
