\v 23 then¦85338 he took us out¦85339 of¦85351 there¦85340, so¦85341 he could bring¦85342 us here to give¦85344 us the¦85348 land¦85348 that¦85349 he'd promised to our¦85351 ancestors¦85351.
\v 24 Yahweh¦85354 ordered¦85353 us to \add ≈follow\add* all¦85358 these¦85361 instructions¦85353 to \add demonstrate\add* that we honour him so that things will go well for¦85367 us and¦85353 \add ≈he'll protect our¦85366 nation as¦85373 he's¦85353 doing¦85355 now\add*.
\v 25 Our¦85392 god¦85392 Yahweh¦85391 \add ≈will¦85377 declare us to¦85379 be innocent of¦85386 wrong\add* if¦85380 we¦85382 obey everything that¦85389 he's¦85394 instructed¦85394 us.’
\c 7
\s1 Warning Yisrael's descendants
\rem /s1 Driving Out the Nations; The Lord's Own People; The Privilege of Holiness; A Chosen People
\r (Exo. 34:11-16)
\p
\v 1 When your¦85416 god¦85400 Yahweh¦85399 brings¦85398 you into¦85401 the land¦85403 which you're¦85406 going¦85407 to¦85409 possess¦85410, he'll¦85398 drive¦85411 out many¦85414 people groups \add ≈ahead¦85416 of¦85416 you\add*: the Hittites¦85417, Girgashites¦85418, Amorites¦85419, Canaanites, Perizzites¦85421, Hivites¦85422, and¦85418 the Yevusites—seven¦85424 \add ≈societies\add* that are¦85407 more¦85428 powerful than¦85428 yourselves.\x + \xo 7:1: \xt Acts 13:19.\x*
\v 2 When¦85430 your¦85432 god¦85432 Yahweh¦85431 \add ≈enables you to¦85433 defeat¦85434\add* them, you \add ≈must kill¦85435 them all\add*. \add ≈You¦85440 must make¦85440 no agreement¦85442 with them\add*, and¦85430 you \add ≈must not¦85438 act mercifully toward\add* them.
\v 3 Don't¦85446 intermarry¦85447 with¦85448 them¦85448: don't¦85446 allow your daughters to marry their sons, or your sons to marry \add any of\add* their daughters
\rem /r (Deuteronomy 7.12-24; 28.1-14)
\v 4 because¦85460 they'd turn¦85462 your¦85465 sons¦85465 away from¦85466 me¦85466, and they'd \add end up\add* serving¦85467 other¦85469 gods¦85468. Then Yahweh¦85473 \add ≈would become very angry\add* with¦85474 you all and would quickly¦85476 destroy¦85475 you.
\v 5 \add ≈What you all should do¦85483\add* to \add @those¦85484 people\add* is to break¦85488 down¦85486 their altars¦85485 and smash their \add stone\add* pillars¦85487, cut¦85490 their Asherah¦85489 poles¦85489 to pieces, and burn¦85492 up their idols¦85491.\x + \xo 7:5: \xt Deu 12:3.\x*
\v 6 \add You must do that\add* because¦85495 you're a¦85496 group of¦85500 people who \add ≈belong only to\add* your¦85500 god¦85505 Yahweh¦85499. \add *He's¦85502\add* chosen¦85502 you \add ≈from¦85510 all¦85510 the people groups in¦85501 the world to be¦85506 his own¦85509 special people\add*.\x + \xo 7:6: \xt Exo 19:5; Deu 4:20; 14:2; 26:18; Tit 2:14; 1Pe 2:9.\x*
\p
\v 7 Yahweh¦85525 loved¦85524 you and¦85527 chose¦85527 you all, not¦85519 because¦85520 you were the \add ≈most populous\add* nation (in¦85526 fact, you were the smallest of all the nations¦85523),
\v 8 but¦85541 because Yahweh loves¦85538 you all and¦85541 because he kept¦85541 the promise that¦85548 he'd made to your ancestors¦85550. Yahweh \add ≈used his power to rescue\add* you all from¦85557 the slavery¦85558 \add imposed by\add* Egypt's¦85563 King¦85561 Far-oh.
\v 9 \add ≈So¦85565 remember\add* that¦85566 your¦85569 god Yahweh¦85568 is God¦85569—the faithful¦85573 god who keeps¦85574 agreements and \add displays\add* loyal¦85576 commitment toward a thousand¦85581 generations¦85582 of¦85577 those¦85578 who love¦85577 him¦85577 and \add ≈obey what he's¦85570 commanded¦85579\add*.\x + \xo 7:9-10: \xt Exo 20:5-6; 34:6-7; Num 14:18; Deu 5:9-10.\x*
\v 10 \add ≈However,\add* to those¦85585 who¦85585 hate¦85585 him¦85585, he¦85591 won't¦85590 hesitate to pay them back with punishment and¦85584 destruction¦85589.
\v 11 \add ≈So¦85600\add* be¦85612 sure to¦85614 obey all the¦85603 instructions¦85606, rules, and¦85600 regulations¦85606 that¦85610 I'm¦85611 giving you¦85612 today.
\s1 Blessings for obedience
