\p
\v 21 Don't¦89199 eat any¦89181 creature that's¦89185 died \add ≈naturally\add*. You may allow foreigners who¦89185 live among you to eat those things. You may also¦89189 sell¦89191 them to other foreigners. But¦89189 you are¦89194 a people¦89194 group that belongs to your¦89198 god¦89198 Yahweh¦89197.
\p You¦89191 mustn't cook a young sheep or¦89190 goat in¦89187 its¦89204 mother's¦89204 milk¦89203.\x + \xo 14:21: \xt Exo 23:19; 34:26.\x*
\rem /s1 The Law of the Tithe; Regulations concerning Tithes; The Giving of Tithes; Tithes
\p
\v 22 \add ≈Make sure\add* you set aside a tenth of¦89210 all¦89210 the¦89212 \add ≈crops that¦89214 you harvest from your fields¦89215\add*.\x + \xo 14:22-29: \xt Lev 27:30-33; Num 18:21.\x*
\v 23 You¦89239 must eat it \add ≈in the presence of\add* your god Yahweh, in the place¦89224 that he'll¦89227 choose¦89227 and \add ≈attach his¦89229 name¦89229 to\add*. That's¦89238 where¦89225 you must eat the tenth of your grain¦89232, wine¦89233, \add olive\add* oil¦89234, and the firstborn¦89235 \add male animals\add* from your herd¦89236 and your flock¦89237, so¦89238 that you'll learn¦89239 to always honour your god Yahweh.
\v 24 When¦89249 \add *he\add* blesses¦89272 you \add with produce\add*, if¦89254 the¦89263 place¦89263 he chooses¦89265 to attach his¦89269 name¦89269 to is too¦89261 far¦89261 for¦89262 you to be¦89251 able¦89256 to carry¦89258 it¦89251 to,
\v 25 then¦89276 you can \add ≈give¦89276 the equivalent in¦89277 cash\add*, and¦89276 \add ≈carefully take¦89278 the cash with¦89277 you all the way\add* to¦89282 the place¦89284 that¦89285 \add *he¦89286\add* chooses¦89286.
\v 26 \add When you get there\add*, \add ≈use the¦89292 money¦89292 to¦89308 purchase any kinds of meat or drink¦89301 that¦89303 you want\add*, and consume it¦89296 there \add ≈in¦89293 front¦89308 of\add* your god¦89310 Yahweh¦89309, and celebrate along with¦89293 your household¦89313.
\p
\v 27 \add Be sure\add* not¦89319 to¦89323 neglect¦89320 any Levites that¦89316 live in¦89318 your¦89318 town, because¦89321 \add ≈they weren't given ancestral land for¦89321 agriculture like you¦89326 were¦89318\add*.
\v 28 At the end¦89329 of every third year, bring¦89333 the tenth of all¦89336 your produce¦89339 for that¦89341 year and¦89342 store¦89342 it in¦89340 your town
\v 29 for the¦89354 Levites¦89346 (because¦89347 they didn't¦89348 get land), and for any foreigners, orphans, and widows¦89356 who¦89357 live in your towns¦89358. They¦89359 can come¦89345 and \add ≈get what they need\add* so¦89361 that your god¦89364 Yahweh¦89363 can bless¦89362 you in everything that you do¦89370.
\c 15
\s1 The 7-year economic reset
\rem /s1 Release for Debtors; Laws concerning the Sabbatical Year; The Seventh Year; The Year for Cancelling Debts
\r (Lev. 25:1-7)
\p
\v 1 At the¦89373 end¦89373 of \add every\add* seven¦89374 years¦89376, you¦89377 must¦89377 \add ≈cancel all debts\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈Handle it like\add* this¦89380: Everyone¦89384 who's loaned money to¦89391 their \add ≈Israeli\add* neighbour¦89391 \add ≈must cancel that debt, i.e.,\add* they must not¦89392 insist that it's paid back, because¦89401 Yahweh¦89405 has¦89403 announced a cancellation.
\v 3 You¦89410 can pressure¦89410 a foreigner¦89409 to¦89413 repay, but¦89411 you¦89417 must¦89410 cancel any debt from a fellow Israeli.
\p
\v 4 However¦89434, there shouldn't¦89422 be¦89423 any poor among¦89425 you, because¦89421 your¦89435 god¦89435 Yahweh¦89431 will¦89430 bless¦89430 you in¦89425 the¦89432 land that¦89433 \add *he's¦89434\add* giving¦89436 you to¦89436 own¦89440 as an¦89439 inheritance¦89439,
\v 5 as long as you listen¦89446 to¦89447 \add ≈what he says\add* and keep following these¦89457 instructions that¦89458 I'm¦89459 telling you today.
\v 6 Because¦89463 your¦89466 god¦89466 Yahweh¦89465 will¦89472 bless¦89467 you (like he promised he would), you'll lend¦89472 to¦89471 many nations rather than borrowing¦89477 from them, and¦89481 you'll rule¦89478 over¦89481 many nations rather than them ruling you.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈In¦89489 the¦89513 towns¦89494\add* that your god¦89499 Yahweh¦89498 is¦89500 giving¦89500 you¦89503, if¦89486 it so happens that any¦89491 of¦89506 your fellow Israelis are poor, then don't¦89502 \add ≈just ignore them and¦89507 refuse to¦89500 help them,\add*\x + \xo 15:7-8: \xt Lev 25:35.\x*
\v 8 but¦89523 instead, open¦89517 your¦89521 \add ≈wallet\add* and¦89523 lend¦89523 them however much they need.
\v 9 \add ≈Be¦89535 careful not to quietly think to yourself¦89532 that the¦89543 seventh-year¦89545 reset\add* is close¦89542 \add so they won't have to pay it back.\add* It¦89548 would be wrong¦89548 not to help a fellow Israeli, and if you did and he¦89555 called¦89555 out¦89555 to Yahweh¦89559 for¦89532 help, then it would be \add ≈counted¦89550 against¦89556 you as disobedience\add*.
\v 10 \add ≈Give¦89564 generously to¦89566 the¦89576 poor without getting resentful inside\add*, because¦89573 then your god¦89580 Yahweh¦89579 can bless¦89578 you¦89565 in¦89571 all your work¦89583 and¦89584 \add ≈all your investments\add*.
\v 11 \add ^There'll always be¦89599 poor people in¦89609 your country¦89606\add*, so¦89597 I¦89598 command¦89599 you¦89599 to give generously¦89601 to the¦89592 poor and needy¦89608 and your fellow Israelis.\x + \xo 15:11: \xt Mat 26:11; Mrk 14:7; Yhn 12:8.\x*
\s1 Freeing slaves
\rem /s1 The Treatment of Slaves; Freeing Servants; Release for Hebrew Slaves
\r (Exo. 21:1-11)
\p
\v 12 If¦89612 a \add ≈fellow Israeli\add* is sold¦89614 to¦89615 you\f + \fr 15:12 \ft Often to pay off their debt.\f* and¦89623 serves¦89620 you for¦89615 six¦89621 years¦89622, then you must¦89614 free¦89626 them in¦89623 the¦89617 seventh¦89624 year¦89623.\x + \xo 15:12-18: \xt Lev 25:39-46.\x*
\v 13 \add ≈But¦89629\add* when¦89629 you¦89633 free¦89632 them, don't¦89634 send¦89635 them off \add ≈empty-handed¦89636\add*
\v 14 \add but instead,\add* give to them generously from your flock¦89641 and from your \add ≈barn\add* and from your wine. \add ≈In whatever ways\add* your god¦89647 Yahweh¦89646 has¦89645 blessed¦89645 you, you should give to them.
\v 15 \add Always\add* remember¦89652 that you were¦89655 a slave¦89654 in¦89656 Egypt¦89657 and¦89652 your¦89665 god¦89660 Yahweh¦89659 redeemed¦89658 you \add out of there\add*, so¦89663 that's¦89653 why I'm¦89664 commanding¦89665 you to do that.
\p
\v 16 \add ≈However¦89678,\add* if¦89673 any slave says¦89675 that they don't¦89677 want to leave you, because¦89673 they \add ≈appreciate\add* you and your¦89684 household¦89684, and so they're better off to stay with¦89689 you,
\v 17 then get¦89691 an awl and \add ≈stand them against the doorpost\add* and pierce one of¦89700 their earlobes with¦89696 the awl, then that person (male or female¦89703) will¦89695 be¦89698 your slave¦89700 forever¦89701.
\v 18 \add ≈Don't complain\add* when¦89712 you have¦89720 to release your slaves, because¦89716 they've served¦89720 you \add up to\add* six¦89721 years¦89722 and¦89723 \add ≈been¦89710 double¦89717 the¦89718 value\add* of¦89718 a \add regular\add* hired¦89719 worker, plus¦89723 your god¦89725 Yahweh¦89724 will¦89723 bless¦89723 you in¦89711 whatever you do¦89728.
\s1 The firstborn animals
