\p
\v 19 You must¦89735 set apart for your god¦89741 Yahweh¦89740, all the firstborn¦89733 male¦89738 animals from your herds and your flocks¦89737. You mustn't use the cattle for working, and mustn't shear¦89747 the sheep¦89749 or goats.\x + \xo 15:19: \xt Exo 13:12.\x*
\v 20 Each¦89761 year¦89755, you¦89754 and your¦89753 household¦89763 must¦89754 \add take them\add* to¦89751 the¦89751 place¦89757 that¦89758 Yahweh¦89752 will¦89754 choose¦89760, and eat¦89754 them there in¦89757 front¦89751 of¦89763 \add *him\add*.
\v 21 \add ≈However,\add* any¦89773 animals that have defects (e.g., lame¦89770 or blind¦89772, or with a severe blemish¦89774) mustn't be¦89767 sacrificed¦89777 to¦89778 your¦89779 god¦89779 Yahweh¦89778.
\v 22 \add Instead,\add* you can eat those \add ≈at home\add* \add ≈whether or not you're ceremonially ‘clean¦89784’\add*, just like¦89786 you'd eat a \add wild\add* gazelle¦89786 or deer¦89787.
\v 23 \add ≈However,\add* don't¦89793 eat¦89794 the blood¦89792—it¦89798 must¦89798 be poured¦89798 out¦89798 on¦89795 the ground like¦89799 water¦89799.\x + \xo 15:23: \xt Gen 9:4; Lev 7:26-27; 17:10-14; 19:26; Deu 12:16-23.\x*
\c 16
\s1 The messenger's ‘pass-over’ celebration
\rem /s1 The Passover; Passover; The Passover Reviewed; Passover and the Festival of Unleavened Bread
\r (Exo. 12:1-20)
\p
\v 1 \add Each year, honour\add* your¦89810 god¦89810 Yahweh¦89809 \add ≈in the early spring\add* by celebrating¦89807 the ‘pass-over¦89808’, because¦89811 it was one night¦89818 \add ≈in the early spring\add* that \add *he¦89814\add* brought¦89814 you¦89814 out¦89814 of¦89816 Egypt¦89817 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*.\x + \xo 16:1-8: \xt Exo 12:1-20; Lev 23:5-8; Num 28:16-25.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈In¦89830 order to celebrate, go to\add* the place¦89826 that your god¦89823 Yahweh¦89822 will¦89829 choose¦89829 \add ≈to attach his¦89832 name¦89832 to\add*, and¦89820 there¦89833 sacrifice¦89820 to \add *him\add* one \add young\add* animal from your flock¦89824 or herd¦89825.
\v 3 Don't eat any leavened¦89839 bread with¦89849 it¦89838. For seven¦89840 days¦89841, you must¦89837 eat flat bread (the bread of suffering) because¦89848 you came¦89861 out¦89850 of Egypt in¦89849 a rush. That's¦89853 how you should¦89854 remember¦89854 the day¦89860 of your exit from¦89862 Egypt for the rest of your life¦89866.
\v 4 \add In fact,\add* for¦89871 seven¦89876 days¦89877 you¦89885 shouldn't¦89868 even have any¦89881 rising agent within your¦89875 borders, and¦89878 none of¦89881 the meat¦89883 from the sacrifice¦89885 on¦89886 that¦89884 first¦89888 evening¦89886 is allowed to¦89889 be¦89870 left until¦89889 the morning¦89889.
\p
\v 5 You¦89892 mustn't sacrifice¦89893 the¦89896 ‘pass-over¦89896’ \add animal\add* within any of¦89897 your towns¦89898 that¦89899 your god¦89902 Yahweh¦89901 is¦89903 giving¦89903 to¦89903 you¦89892—
\v 6 only at the place¦89911 that¦89912 your god¦89916 Yahweh¦89915 will¦89920 choose¦89914 to \add ≈attach his¦89918 name¦89918 to\add*. That's where you¦89920 must¦89914 sacrifice¦89920 the ‘pass-over¦89923’ \add animal\add* at sunset, which¦89912 was the time¦89927 when \add ≈your ancestors\add* started leaving Egypt¦89929.
\v 7 You¦89931 must¦89931 cook¦89931 the meat and¦89931 eat¦89932 it¦89938 at¦89933 the place¦89933 that¦89934 Yahweh¦89936 will¦89939 choose¦89935, then¦89931 in¦89933 the morning¦89940 you¦89941 can \add start\add* returning¦89941 to¦89942 your¦89942 \add ≈homes\add*.
\v 8 Then for six days¦89945 you¦89946 must¦89946 only eat¦89946 flat bread¦89947, and¦89948 the¦89948 seventh¦89949 day is a special celebration for your¦89952 god¦89952 Yahweh¦89951—don't¦89953 do¦89954 any work¦89955 on¦89948 that day.
\s1 The harvest celebration
