\r (Exo. 34:22; Lev. 23:15-21)
\p
\v 9 You¦89960 must¦89960 count¦89960 off seven¦89968 weeks¦89969 \add ≈starting from¦89963 when¦89963 the very first¦89963 harvesting of grain¦89965 begins¦89966\add*.\x + \xo 16:9-12: \xt Lev 23:15-21; Num 28:26-31.\x*
\v 10 Then¦89971 celebrate¦89971 the ‘Festival¦89983 of¦89972 Weeks¦89973’\f + \fr 16:10 \ft Also known as the ‘Harvest Festival’ or ‘Pentecost’ (relating to the fifty days = seven weeks plus one day).\f* \add to honour\add* your¦89975 god¦89984 Yahweh¦89974 by contributing a¦89976 freewill¦89977 offering¦89977 \add acknowledging\add* however much \add *he¦89982\add* has blessed¦89982 you¦89971.
\v 11 You¦89986 should celebrate in Yahweh's¦89989 presence, along with¦89998 your children and your servants¦89994, and any Levites¦89996 living in your town, and the foreigners, orphans, and widows¦90001 living among you¦89986. Take your offerings to the place¦90004 that¦90002 your god¦90008 Yahweh will¦90006 choose¦90006 \add ≈to attach his¦90010 name¦90010 to\add*.
\v 12 \add Always\add* remember¦90013 that¦90014 you¦90017 were¦90017 a slave¦90016 in¦90018 Egypt¦90018, \add ≈so carefully¦90019 follow those¦90024 instructions¦90023\add*.
\s1 The celebration in temporary huts
\rem /s1 The Festival of Shelters; The Festival of Booths Reviewed; Feast of Tabernacles
\r (Lev. 23:33-43)
\p
\v 13 \add After\add* you've¦90033 brought in¦90033 the grain harvest and¦90035 pressed out the grape juice, you must¦90029 celebrate the ‘Festival¦90027 of¦90031 Shelters’ for¦90030 seven¦90031 days¦90032.\x + \xo 16:13-15: \xt Lev 23:33-36,39-43; Num 29:12-38.\x*
\v 14 You¦90037 should celebrate along with¦90038 your children and your servants¦90042, as well as any Levites¦90044 and foreigners and orphans and widows¦90047 who¦90048 live in¦90038 your town.
\v 15 \add Honour\add* your god¦90055 Yahweh¦90054 at¦90056 the¦90068 place¦90056 \add *he'll¦90059\add* choose¦90059, by celebrating¦90053 for¦90061 seven days¦90052 because¦90061 \add *he's¦90062\add* blessed¦90062 your harvest and¦90067 \add ≈all¦90065 your other work¦90068\add*.
\p
\v 16 \add In summary,\add* all your men must¦90078 travel three times¦90075 each year¦90077 to the place¦90088 that¦90089 your god¦90087 Yahweh¦90086 will¦90090 choose¦90090: at the Flat Bread¦90092 Celebration, at the Festival of Weeks¦90094, and¦90095 at the Festival of Shelters. \add ≈No man should come empty-handed¦90103\add*,
\v 17 \add but rather,\add* each man \add ≈must give in proportion\add* to¦90106 the¦90106 blessings¦90108 that your¦90110 god¦90110 Yahweh¦90109 has¦90112 given¦90112 you \add during that year\add*.
\s1 Strive for justice
\rem /s1 Municipal Judges and Officers; Justice for the People; Judges; The Administration of Justice
\p
\v 18 You¦90119 must appoint¦90119 judges¦90117 and other officials¦90118 throughout your tribes¦90130, in¦90122 all¦90122 the towns¦90124 that¦90125 your god¦90127 Yahweh¦90126 is¦90128 giving¦90128 to¦90128 you¦90119. They¦90131 must judge¦90131 the people¦90134 \add ≈fairly and correctly\add*.
\v 19 You¦90141 mustn't \add ≈pervert¦90155 justice¦90142 or give favours\add*. Don't¦90143 accept bribes¦90149 because¦90150 a bribe¦90151 causes \add an otherwise\add* wise¦90154 person to¦90144 \add ≈ignore evil\add* and¦90155 \add ≈misrepresents what innocent people say\add*.\x + \xo 16:19: \xt Exo 23:6-8; Lev 19:15.\x*
\v 20 \add ≈True justice is what you should¦90163 aim for¦90173\add*, so¦90162 that you'll¦90161 occupy and¦90164 live¦90163 in the¦90167 land¦90167 that your¦90171 god¦90171 Yahweh¦90170 is giving¦90172 you.
\s1 Prohibitions in worship and justice
