\p
\v 21 Never put an¦90180 Asherah¦90180 pole¦90180 near the¦90185 altar¦90185 to¦90179 your¦90187 god¦90187 Yahweh¦90186 that¦90188 you'll¦90178 build for¦90191 yourself¦90179,\x + \xo 16:21: \xt Exo 34:13.\x*
\v 22 and¦90194 don't¦90194 erect any stone pillars¦90198 that¦90199 your¦90202 god¦90202 Yahweh¦90201 hates¦90200.\x + \xo 16:22: \xt Lev 26:1.\x*
\c 17
\p
\v 1 Don't¦90221 sacrifice¦90207 any \add ≈animal\add* to¦90208 your¦90209 god¦90209 Yahweh¦90208 that has any blemish¦90215 or defect, because¦90219 \add *he¦90220\add* detests that.
\p
\v 2 In¦90248 any of¦90229 the towns¦90231 that your¦90229 god¦90235 Yahweh¦90234 is¦90236 giving¦90236 you, if¦90226 you discover any man¦90238 or¦90239 woman¦90241 who¦90242 does¦90243 evil¦90246 by¦90251 disobeying the agreement¦90252 that \add *he's¦90243\add* made with¦90229 you
\v 3 and¦90254 \add ≈worshipped¦90258\add* other¦90257 gods¦90256, or the¦90267 sun¦90260, moon¦90263, or stars—all of¦90267 which¦90269 I've¦90272 prohibited you from¦90265 doing,\x + \xo 17:3: \xt Exo 22:20.\x*
\v 4 and it it's reported to¦90276 you, and you listen¦90277 and investigate¦90278 it thoroughly¦90279, and it's true that¦90286 this¦90286 detestable¦90285 thing¦90285 was done¦90284 in¦90287 Yisrael¦90287,
\v 5 you¦90289 must¦90289 bring¦90289 that¦90305 man¦90292 or¦90294 woman¦90297 out¦90289 to¦90306 the¦90292 \add town\add* gates¦90308, and¦90289 \add ≈execute them by throwing rocks¦90317 at¦90317 them\add*.
\v 6 \add Note that\add* that person can only be executed¦90329 if there's at least two¦90324 witnesses¦90336 \add as evidence\add*—no one can be put¦90332 to¦90332 death¦90332 on¦90333 the¦90335 testimony of¦90335 just one witness¦90325.\x + \xo 17:6: \xt Num 35:30; Deu 19:15; Mat 18:16; 2Cor 13:1; 1Tim 5:19; Heb 10:28.\x*
\v 7 \add ≈The¦90340 witnesses¦90340 must¦90341 be¦90341 the ones to throw the first¦90344 rocks\add* then all¦90347 the other people¦90349 after that, and¦90351 that's how you'll¦90351 remove¦90351 evil¦90352 \add ≈from¦90353 your¦90353 society\add*.\x + \xo 17:7: \xt 1Cor 5:13.\x*
\rem /s1 Law Courts; Legal Decisions by Priests and Judges
\p
\v 8 If¦90356 a¦90361 case¦90376 is too¦90357 difficult¦90357 for¦90358 you yourselves to judge¦90362 \add ≈(e.g., two parties claiming¦90371 bloodshed¦90365, or lawsuits, or assaults¦90374, or other disputes¦90370 within your towns¦90377)\add*, you must¦90357 leave town and¦90379 go¦90379 to the¦90382 place¦90382 that¦90383 your god¦90386 Yahweh¦90385 is going to choose¦90384.
\v 9 You¦90389 should go¦90389 to the \add ≈Levitical¦90393 priests¦90392\add* and to the judge¦90396 \add ≈on duty there\add* and they¦90402 will¦90401 \add ≈produce\add* a judgement.
\v 10 Whatever the decision¦90412 is that's made at the place¦90418 Yahweh¦90422 will¦90414 choose¦90421, \add ≈that's the verdict that must¦90408 be applied to¦90425 the case\add*—
\v 11 accept their judgement and¦90435 do¦90442 what they¦90434 say¦90440 without making any adjustments to¦90441 their decision¦90437.
\v 12 Anyone who \add ≈shows\add* contempt¦90459 for \add the decision of\add* the judge¦90475 or¦90472 the priest¦90464 who's¦90456 standing¦90465 there¦90467 serving¦90466 your¦90471 god¦90471 Yahweh¦90470, then¦90455 that person¦90455 must¦90458 be executed \add ≈to¦90460\add* remove¦90479 that evil¦90480 from¦90481 Yisrael¦90481,
\v 13 then¦90483 all¦90483 the¦90485 people¦90485 will¦90486 hear¦90486 \add about it\add* and be afraid¦90487, and \add ≈it'll stamp out such arrogance\add*.
\s1 Expectations for a king
\rem /s1 Limitations of Royal Authority; The King; Guidelines for a King; Instructions concerning a King
\p
\v 14 When you enter the land¦90498 that your¦90501 god¦90501 Yahweh¦90500 is¦90502 about¦90502 to¦90502 give¦90502 you, then occupy and live in¦90506 it¦90506, and you say¦90507 that you need a king¦90510 over¦90509 you like¦90511 all¦90511 the surrounding countries¦90513 have,\x + \xo 17:14: \xt 1Sam 8:5.\x*
\v 15 you can appoint¦90518 the¦90526 king over¦90525 you that¦90537 Yahweh¦90523 chooses¦90522. Your¦90527 king must¦90518 be¦90532 \add ≈an Israeli\add*—\add ≈never allow a foreigner¦90536 to¦90533 become your¦90527 king\add*.
\v 16 However, he mustn't acquire a large number of horses for¦90548 himself, and¦90550 he should never send people¦90555 to Egypt¦90556 to buy horses, because Yahweh¦90560 has¦90561 told you all to never go back that¦90567 way¦90566 again¦90568.\x + \xo 17:16: \xt 1Ki 10:28; 2Ch 1:16; 9:28.\x*
\v 17 He¦90571 mustn't \add ≈take a lot of¦90577 wives¦90574 for¦90583 himself\add* \add ≈or else he might stop\add* \add worshipping Yahweh\add*. Nor should he \add ≈accumulate too much\add* gold¦90579 and¦90570 silver¦90578.\x + \xo 17:17: a \xt 1Ki 11:1-8; \xo b \xt 1Ki 10:14-22,27; 2Ch 1:15; 9:27.\x*
\p
\v 18 Once he's¦90587 sitting¦90587 on his¦90590 \add ≈royal\add* throne¦90589, he must¦90591 copy¦90595 for¦90601 himself the instructions on the scroll¦90600 \add ≈that's in the custody of¦90589\add* the Levitical¦90603 priests¦90602,
\v 19 then¦90605 he must¦90605 keep it with¦90606 him¦90606 and read¦90607 \add some of\add* it every day¦90611 so¦90613 that¦90627 he learns¦90614 to honour his¦90619 god¦90619 Yahweh¦90618—being¦90605 careful to follow all¦90623 the¦90625 instructions¦90630 and regulations¦90630 written in¦90608 it
\v 20 so that he won't¦90634 \add ≈think he's¦90647 more¦90638 valued than¦90638 his fellow citizens\add*, and so that he doesn't \add ≈ignore those instructions even slightly\add*. \add ≈As a result, him and his descendants¦90653 will rule as kings in¦90654 Yisrael¦90655 for many years\add*.
\c 18
\s1 Portions for Levites
\rem /s1 Offerings for Priests and Levites; Privileges of Priests and Levites; Gifts for the Priests and Levites; The Share of the Priests
\p
\v 1 None of¦90663 the Levites¦90662 (including¦90668 the priests¦90661) will receive \add any land as\add* an¦90668 inheritance like the \add ≈other Israelis¦90671\add*. \add ≈Instead, the people's offerings¦90672 to Yahweh¦90673 will be their¦90674 inheritance to sustain them\add*.
\v 2 \add Yes,\add* unlike \add ≈fellow Israelis\add*, they won't¦90678 have any inherited¦90677 \add land\add*—Yahweh¦90685 is¦90687 their inheritance¦90687 like he¦90689 told them.\x + \xo 18:2: \xt Num 18:20.\x*
\p
\v 3 This¦90694 is¦90695 the requirement that¦90694 the people¦90699 do for the priests¦90697: whenever they bring a bull¦90705 or¦90706 a sheep¦90708 as a sacrifice¦90701, they must¦90695 give¦90709 the shoulder¦90711, the cheeks¦90712, and¦90712 the stomach¦90713 to¦90710 the priest¦90710.
\v 4 Also you¦90722 must¦90722 give¦90722 \add @the Levites¦90724\add* the firstfruits¦90715 of¦90715 your grain¦90716, your grape juice, your \add olive\add* oil¦90718, and¦90719 the wool shorn from your sheep¦90721,
