\v 9 \add ≈So\add* follow all the instructions in this agreement and¦96200 obey the rules so that you'll all prosper in everything¦96201 you do.
\p
\v 10 All of you stand \add here\add* today \add ≈in¦96210 front\add* of your god Yahweh: your chiefs, your tribes, your elders, and¦96208 your officers, all the¦96210 Israeli men
\v 11 along with¦96220 your¦96222 wives and children, and the¦96229 foreigners \add ≈living\add* among you (who cut wood and fetch water for you),
\v 12 to enter into¦96244 an agreement with your¦96251 god¦96244 Yahweh, and¦96249 to \add accept\add* the¦96236 promise that¦96249 \add ≈he's¦96240 made to\add* you¦96235 today.
\v 13 That will establish \add @your country¦96260\add* as his people, and he will be¦96261 your god as he told you¦96259 he would, having promised \add >it\add* to your ancestors Abraham, Yitshak, and Yakov.
\v 14 This¦96282 agreement isn't¦96286 just with¦96273 all of¦96281 you here¦96287 today,
\v 15 the¦96306 ones standing here, \add ≈but¦96302 also¦96302\add* with those who aren't here with you today.
\p
\v 16 You all know how we lived in Egypt, and¦96312 then travelled through other \add ≈kingdoms\add* on our way \add here\add*,
\v 17 and you've all seen their disgusting practices and the¦96342 idols that¦96339 they had, made of¦96345 wood and stone, gold and silver.
\v 18 If¦96377 there happens to be a man or woman, or clan or tribe, whose \add ≈loyalty\add* is turning away¦96382 today from your god Yahweh¦96380 and to go and serve those gods in¦96364 those other nations, i.e., if¦96377 there's a \add ≈bitter or poisonous root\add* among you all,\x + \xo 29:18: \xt Heb 12:15.\x*
\v 19 and if¦96395 they hear the words of¦96400 this¦96411 curse¦96408, then¦96396 they'll think to¦96393 themselves, ‘We'll have peace, even though \add ≈our minds are fixed on¦96402 where we're going\add*,’ so that¦96409 the \add ?≈good and the bad are carried along together\add*,
\v 20 Yahweh won't be willing to forgive them. \add No,\add* his jealousy and anger will rage against them, and all¦96424 the¦96425 curses written¦96430 in¦96431 this¦96433 book¦96431 will land on¦96431 them, and Yahweh will wipe out their name \add ≈never to be remembered again\add*.
\v 21 Then Yahweh¦96460 will¦96441 single out that person \add or group\add* from¦96446 all of Yisrael's tribe, to be marked out for disaster as per all the¦96452 curses that are written in¦96461 this book of instructions.
\p
\v 22 Then a future generation (your descendants who'll be born in¦96477 the future, plus¦96465 the foreigner who comes¦96476 from a distant land), when they see the \add ≈terrible problems\add* \add that hit\add* that land and¦96472 the diseases that Yahweh¦96489 \add sent to\add* make it¦96476 sick, will say,
\v 23 ‘All¦96495 that¦96505 land¦96504 is¦96507 sulfur and burning salt. No one plants anything and nothing sprouts, and not even grass grows in it, like the¦96507 overthrow of¦96507 Sodom and Amorah \add !(Gomorrah)\add*, Admah and Tsevoim, which Yahweh¦96502 destroyed in his rage and anger¦96508,’\x + \xo 29:23: \xt Gen 19:24-25.\x*
\v 24 and¦96513 all the¦96519 nations will¦96513 \add ≈ask\add*, ‘Why did Yahweh¦96520 do that to that country? What's \add ≈he¦96524 so angry about¦96519\add*?’
\v 25 Then \add ≈others¦96535 will reply\add*, ‘Because they¦96532 neglected their agreement with Yahweh, the god of their ancestors, that¦96540 he \add ≈made\add* with them when he brought them out from Egypt,
\v 26 and they went and served other gods and bowed down to them—gods that¦96562 they hadn't \add ≈heard of¦96559 before or had anything to do with¦96563\add*.
