\p
\v 11 These instructions that¦96814 I'm¦96815 giving you today aren't¦96818 too¦96820 difficult¦96820 or \add ≈impractical\add* for¦96822 you—
\v 12 it's¦96829 not like you have to send someone up¦96832 to heaven¦96835 to get them so¦96836 you can hear¦96838 them and¦96838 follow them.\x + \xo 30:12-14: \xt Rom 10:6-8.\x*
\v 13 Nor are¦96844 they on the opposite side¦96844 of¦96845 the ocean such that¦96848 you have to find someone to cross¦96849 over¦96849 to get them so¦96858 you can hear¦96858 them and¦96842 follow them.
\v 14 \add On the contrary,\add* these instructions are¦96864 very¦96867 close¦96864 to¦96870 you—you \add ≈should discuss them and¦96869 think about¦96868 them\add* so that you can follow them.
\s1 The selection of life
\p
\v 15 Listen, I've placed \add the choice between\add* life¦96879 and good¦96882, and death¦96885 and evil¦96888, in front¦96875 of you today.
\v 16 What I'm¦96891 commanding¦96892 you today is¦96894 to love¦96894 your god Yahweh, to walk in his ways¦96900 and to follow his instructions¦96903 and \add ≡obey\add* his rules and regulations¦96903, and then you'll¦96905 live¦96905 and multiply¦96906, and your god Yahweh will¦96907 bless¦96907 you in the¦96910 land that¦96890 you're¦96913 about¦96914 to \add ≈take¦96917 possession¦96917 of¦96917\add*.
\v 17 But¦96919 if¦96919 your¦96922 \add ≈loyalty shifts\add* away and you don't¦96923 listen¦96924 \add ≈but¦96919 instead\add* you're drawn¦96925 away and bow¦96926 down¦96926 to¦96927 other¦96928 gods¦96927 and serve¦96929 them¦96929,
\v 18 \add then\add* I'm warning you all today that¦96934 you'll all \add ≈most certainly¦96935\add* die, i.e., you won't¦96937 live for¦96932 a long time¦96940 in the land which¦96934 you're¦96945 about¦96946 to cross¦96946 the Yarden¦96949 \add river\add* to \add ≈take¦96953 possession¦96953 of¦96953\add*.
